  - hybrid solvers
  - domain decomposition
  - finite element methods

abstract: >-
  The primary objective is to develop an FE-NO coupling framework using domain decomposition framework. 
  In this framework, a pretrained deep operator network (DeepONet) is employed to efficiently resolve complex, 
  nonlinear subdomains specifically replacing the locations where fine meshes are requires, 
  while the Finite Element Method (FEM) handles the remaining regions. Capturing strongly nonlinear behaviors with FEM alone 
  is computationally expensive. In contrast, DeepONet represent nonlinear mappings that can be pretrained offline, 
  making their evaluation during simulation essentially negligible in cost. In this work, the DeepONet is trained with 
  the physics of the system only (no data is used). The coupling of the two solvers is expected to leverage their complementary 
  strengths, leading to a significant enhancement in computational efficiency and robustness while maintaining solution accuracy.

